    "ls|LS16_S6_U_192": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nDEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 192\nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 11TH DECEMBER 2015\nAMRIT PROGRAMME\n*192. SHRI MOHITE PATIL VIJAYSINH SHANKARRAO:\nSHRI RAHUL SHEWALE:\nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Government has launched the Affordable Medicines and Reliable\nImplant Treatment (AMRIT) pharmacy Scheme across the country;\n(b) if so, the details , status and salient features thereof along with the name of the\ndiseases covered and the medicines proposed to be provided thereunder; and\n(c) the number of such pharmacies opened/proposed to be opened across the country,\nState/UT-wise including Maharashtra along with the time by which the said pharmacies\nare likely to be fully operational across the country?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\n(SHRI JAGAT PRAKASH NADDA)\n(a) to (c):  A statement is laid on the Table of the House\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 192* FOR 11TH DECEMBER, 2015\n(a) to (c): Affordable Medicines and Reliable Implant Treatment (AMRIT) pharmacy\nhas been opened at All India Institute of Medical Sciences (AIIMS), New Delhi and is\napproved for six new AIIMS and major Central Government hospitals. The State/UT\nwise list of the hospitals/institutions where such pharmacies are approved is placed at\nAnnexure 1.\nAMRIT pharmacies are to sell Cancer and Cardiovascular disease drugs and\nimplants to the patient s with valid prescriptions. The list of the medicine s and implants\nidentified for Cancer and Cardiovascular Diseases for AMRIT Outlet at AIIMS, New\nDelhi is placed at Annexure 2.\nState Governments have been informed regarding A MRIT pharmacies and M/s\nHLL Lifecare Ltd. has been directed to consider the request s of State Governments for\nopening of AMRIT pharmacies at major State Government hospitals/Institutions.