    "ls|LS16_S6_U_205": "LOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 205 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 14.12.2015 \n \nPNG/CNG DISTRIBUTION BY PRIVATE COMPANIES \n \n \n* 205.     SHRI RAMDAS C. TADAS: \n  \nWill the Minister of PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS be pleased to state: \n \nisVªksfy;e vkSj izkd`frd xSl ea=h \n \n(a) the existing mechanism of distribution of PNG/CNG in the country;  \n \n(b) whether the Government proposes to carry out distribution and sale of PNG and CNG gas through \nprivate companies and if so, the details thereof along with the names of such companie s and cities \ninvolved in such distribution;  \n \n(c) whether the Government has allowed some private companies to construct gas pipeline in the \ncountry;  \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof and the number of contracts for construction of gas pipeline awarded by \nthe Government to private companies, project/company and State/UT -wise including Maharashtra; \nand  \n \n(e) the efforts made by the Government to decontrol the PNG/CNG gas sector in order to provide \nclean and cheap fuel and supply to domestic/industrial use in the country? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nपेट्रोलियम और प्राकृलिक गैस मंत्रािय में राज् य मंत्ररी (स् विंत्र प्राार  \n(श्ररी धमेन्‍द र प्रधान     \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN THE MINISTRY OF PETROLEUM \n& NATURAL GAS (SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n(a) to (e): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (e) OF THE LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.205 ASKED BY SHRI RAMDAS C. TADAS, MP TO BE \nANSWERED ON DECEMBER 14, 2015 \n(a): Distribution of Compressed Natural Gas (CNG)/ Piped Natural Gas (PNG) for domestic, \ncommercial and Industrial usage is carried out by City Gas Distribution (CGD) network. In year 2007, \nGovernment has established Petroleum and Natural Gas Regulatory Board (PNGRB) under the \nPNGRB Act 2006.  Under  the Act, PNGRB grants the authorization to the entities for developing a \nCGD network in a specified Geographical Area (GA) of the country.  This authorization is granted in \nterms of the provisions of the PNGRB Act 2006 and the relevant regulations notifie d thereunder, \nnamely, PNGRB (Authorizing entities to Lay, Build, Operate or Expand City or Local Natural Gas \nDistribution Networks) Regulations, 2008.    \n \n(b) to (d):  Granting of authorization for development of CGD network to supply CNG/PNG in a \nspecified GA is being carried out in a transparent manner by the PNGRB as provided in the Act.  \nPNGRB follows the bidding process to select the entities for granting authorization to develop CGD \nnetwork. Bids can be submitted by either a private company or a public company subject to qualifying \nthe bidder evaluation criteria as referred to in PNGRB (Authorizing entities to Lay, Build, Operate or \nExpand City or Local Natural Gas Distribution Networks) Regulations, 2008.  PNGRB is only \ngranting authorization to entit ies for development of CGD network and subsequent contracts for \nconstruction of gas pipeline/CGD network are being awarded by the concerned authorized entities. In \nthe State of Maharashtra, the following four entities are developing CGD networks in differe nt \ncities/GAs.  \ni)  Mahanagar Gas Limited (MGL)   - Mumbai, Greater Mumbai, Thane  \n       City and adjoining areas, Raigarh. \nii) Maharashtra Natural Gas limited (MNGL) - Pune City \niii) Gujarat Gas Limited (GGL)   - Thane District (excluding areas of  \n       MGL) \niv) Mahesh Resources Private Limited   - Pune District (excluding areas of  \n       MNGL \nThe details of the entities which are carrying out distribution of CNG/PNG in the country are at \nAnnexure-I.  \n(e): Government has accorded highest priority in do mestic gas allocation to PNG (Domestic) and \nCNG (Transport) segments of CGD networks in order to faster rollout of PNG/CNG networks.  The \nentire gas requirement of CNG (Transport) and PNG (Domestic) is being met by supply of domestic \ngas. The selection of granting authorization to develop CGD network is being done based on \ncompetitive bidding process. Maximum Retail Prices of CNG/PNG are being fixed by concerned \nentities as provided under the PNGRB Act, 2006 and Government does not fix/regulate the prices o f \nCNG/PNG supplies. \n***** \n\nANNEXURE-I REFERRED IN REPLY TO PART (b) to (d) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 205 TO BE ANSWERED ON 14.12.2015 REGARDING PNG/CNG \nDISTRIBUTION BY PRIVATE COMPANIES \nDetails of existing City Gas Distribution networks across the country as on 1st October, 2015 \nS. \nN.  State Name of \nGeographical Area \n     \nNo. of consumers     \n \n CNG \nStations \nPNG           \n(Domestic)  \nPNG \n(Ind.)  \n  PNG          \n(Comm.)  \n1 Telangana Hyderabad 947 3 5 20 \n2 \nAndhra \nPradesh \nVijayawada 282 0 3 8 \n3 Kakinada 2519 0 38 4 \n4 East Godavari* 0 0 0 0 \n5 West Godavari* 0 0 0 0 \n6 Krishna* 0 0 0 0 \n7 Assam Upper Assam 28985 392 1037 0 \n8 Delhi Delhi 440981 307 1170 278 \n9 \nGujarat \nAhmedabad 210536 690 1430 47 \n  Vadodara 556 84 0 6 \n10 Anand 20750 108 531 0 \n11 Vadodara 78035 17 2604 8 \n12 Hazira 29830  13   86  1 \n13 Jamnagar 256  1   -    5 \n14 Nadiad 49451  13   259  9 \n15 Navsari 79817  42   115  10 \n16 Rajkot 151360  1,045   730  31 \n17 Surendernagar 19958  274   135  15 \n18 Valsad 81805  543   155  19 \n19 Khambhat 27964  6   149  5 \n20 Halol 8491  58   39  7 \n  Gandhinagar 95332  20   389  9 \n21 Palej 0  10   -    2 \n22 Kutch (West)* 0 0 0 0 \n  Out of GA 0  3   -    53 \n23 Bhavnagar 218  -     -    8 \n24 Surat-Bharuch-\nAnklashwer 492098  764   9,550  61 \n  Ahmedabad 0 0 0 22 \n25 Gandhinagar- \nMehsana-Sabarkantha 91862 248 475 43 \n26 Kutch (East)* 0 0 0 0 \n27 \nHaryana \nFaridabad 15342 161 32 10 \n28 Sonipat 5383 30 8 3 \n29 Gurgaon 7585 13 63 7 \n30 Panipat* 0 0 0 0 \n\n31 \nMadhya \nPradesh \nGwalior 204 1 0 2 \n32 Indore (including \nUjjain) 4262 55 36 16 \n33 Dewas  831 25 2 1 \n34 \n& \n35 \nMaharashtra \nMumb